%% SignFlow — PROPOSED partner integration (NOT implemented yet)
%% Planned = Partner API, partner auth, sign requests, launch codes, trust/revocation, outbox, webhooks.
%% Reused  = invitations (hashed tokens), guest signing session, server-side PDF validation, revision storage.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    box rgb(228,237,248) Coworker's system
        actor BU as Business user
        participant WA as Coworker web app
        participant CB as Coworker backend
        participant WH as Coworker webhook endpoint
    end
    participant BR as User's browser
    box rgb(221,241,238) SignFlow server
        participant PA as Partner REST API (planned)
        participant PZ as Partner authN/authZ (planned)
        participant SR as Signing request service (planned)
        participant IS as Invitation service (exists)
        participant DB as PostgreSQL
        participant OS as PDF storage
        participant IP as Web invitation page /invitations/{token} (exists)
        participant VS as Signature validation (exists, + trust policy planned)
        participant OB as Webhook outbox + dispatcher (planned)
    end
    box rgb(248,227,225) User's PC
        participant D as SignFlow Desktop (JavaFX)
        participant P as Local PKCS#35;11 provider
        participant C as USB token / smart card
    end

    Note over CB,PA: Trust boundary 1: partner API key / client credential lives ONLY in the coworker backend.<br/>Never in the browser or the desktop app.

    BU->>WA: Clicks "Approve contract"
    WA->>CB: Approve request (user session of the coworker app)
    CB->>CB: Business rules: contract ready? who must sign?

    CB->>PA: POST /api/partner/v1/sign-requests (HTTPS, multipart PDF + metadata, Idempotency-Key)
    PA->>PZ: Authenticate partner credential, check scope sign_requests:create
    alt Invalid or revoked credential
        PZ-->>CB: 401 / 403
    else Authorised
        PA->>SR: Create request (partnerId, externalRef, signer, callbackUrl, returnUrl)
        SR->>SR: Validate PDF (size, parseable, not encrypted), returnUrl on partner allow-list
        SR->>OS: Store original PDF
        SR->>IS: Create one-signer workflow + invitation
        IS->>DB: sign_requests (status PENDING, document SHA-256, expiry), invitations (token SHA-256 only)
        SR-->>PA: id, status, expiresAt, signUrl
        PA-->>CB: 201 Created { id, status, expiresAt, signUrl }
    end

    CB-->>WA: signUrl
    WA-->>BR: Redirect to signUrl
    BR->>IP: GET /invitations/{token}
    alt Expired, revoked or already used
        IP-->>BR: Friendly page "link expired / ask sender"
    else Valid
        IP->>DB: Create launch code (random, single use, about 2 minutes, bound to invitation)
        IP-->>BR: Page: "Open in SignFlow" (signflow://launch/{code}) or "Download SignFlow"
    end

    BR->>D: signflow://launch/{code} (OS protocol handler)
    Note over D: Trust boundary 2: the deep link carries only an opaque code.<br/>Desktop ignores any URL, id or data in it and uses its configured server.
    D->>PA: POST /api/launch/exchange { code } (HTTPS)
    PA->>DB: Consume code atomically (unused, not expired)
    alt Code invalid, reused or expired
        PA-->>D: 401
        D-->>BU: "Link expired, open it again from the email or website"
    else OK
        PA-->>D: Signing-session JWT scoped to ONE request and ONE signer slot (short TTL)
    end

    D->>PA: GET signing task + PDF (Bearer signing-session JWT)
    PA->>OS: Read PDF
    PA-->>D: Request details + PDF
    D->>D: Show document, partner name, reason

    D->>P: Detect token, list certificates (no PIN)
    alt Token missing or disconnected
        P-->>D: Error
        D-->>BU: "Insert your card" (retry)
    else Present
        BU->>D: Select certificate, confirm "Ready to Sign"
        BU->>D: Enter PIN
        D->>P: C_Login, then C_Sign over CMS signed attributes
        P->>C: Sign inside the chip
        Note over C: Trust boundary 3: private key never leaves the token. PIN never leaves the PC.
        C-->>D: Signature
        D->>D: Build signed PDF (incremental), verify locally
    end

    alt User rejects / cancels
        D->>PA: POST decline (optional reason)
        PA->>SR: Status DECLINED
        SR->>OB: Outbox event sign_request.declined
    else Signs
        D->>PA: POST signed PDF (parent hash, signingOperationId)
        PA->>VS: Validate before accepting
        VS->>VS: Incremental update of original, crypto valid, cert = bound or allowed,<br/>chain to trusted CA, OCSP/CRL revocation per policy
        alt Upload failed (network)
            D->>PA: Retry with same signingOperationId (idempotent)
        else Invalid signature, untrusted or revoked certificate
            VS-->>PA: Rejected
            PA-->>D: 422 with reason, status unchanged
        else Valid
            VS->>OS: Store signed PDF (immutable)
            VS->>DB: One transaction: status SIGNED + signed PDF SHA-256 + audit event + outbox row
            PA-->>D: 200 Signed
            D-->>BU: Success, "Back to contract app" (opens allow-listed returnUrl)
        end
    end

    Note over OB,WH: Asynchronous from here: delivery never blocks the signer.
    loop Until delivered or max retries (exponential backoff)
        OB-)WH: POST webhook {eventId, type, requestId, externalRef}<br/>X-SignFlow-Timestamp + HMAC-SHA256 signature
        alt 2xx
            WH-->>OB: Acknowledged, outbox row DELIVERED
        else Timeout / 5xx
            WH-->>OB: Failed, schedule retry
        end
    end
    WH->>WH: Verify HMAC + timestamp window, skip duplicate eventId (idempotent)
    WH->>CB: Mark contract as signed (business record)
    CB->>PA: GET /api/partner/v1/sign-requests/{id}/document (partner credential)
    PA->>PZ: Request belongs to this partner?
    alt Not owner or not yet SIGNED
        PZ-->>CB: 404 / 409
    else OK
        PA->>OS: Read signed PDF
        PA-->>CB: Signed PDF + SHA-256
    end
    opt Webhook never arrived
        CB->>PA: GET /api/partner/v1/sign-requests/{id} (polling fallback)
    end
